tasks.description:
Apple's App Store Server API answers 401 to every production call until an app has a production release (https://github.com/apple/app-store-server-library-node/issues/60: "Apps without a production release are not authorized to call any production endpoints"). Twelve tries on 2026-10-08 got 401; the sandbox test passed end to end (Cawrier verified it, and its forward to Yield got 200).

At CawCo's first App Store release:
- call `POST https://api.storekit.itunes.apple.com/inApps/v1/notifications/test` with an App Store Server API token signed by the team key 5JW54DXB77 that carries `bid: "dev.cawco.app"`. `~/asc.py` on the Mac signs ASC tokens without `bid`, so add an optional bid argument to it for this;
- confirm Cawrier logs the verified TEST notification and the Yield forward's 200;
- confirm Yield shows it under Notifications.

DESIGN.md's Open Page Rule (almost no blocking dialog or sheet; answer in place, on the row it was asked from). The web moved its remaining modal confirms in place (464cb194, and leaf 2f8e29eb finishing the rest). On iOS, ConfirmDialog( still opens at:
- SessionMenus.swift:95, :108, :124, :194 (Delete transcript, Remove session, Discard; they open from their row via KitDialogController.origin, but are still a dialog);
- Machines.swift:671;
- NewSessionPickers.swift:534 ("Switch to Full Send?").
ShellController.swift:1483 (Forget project) belongs to the iOS project-views leaf 67c5a474, and ActsProbe.swift:224 is a DEBUG probe; leave both. Match each flow to the web's in-place equivalent once 2f8e29eb lands (read the web flow first: same words, same states, same refusal handling, via SessionActs), and delete ConfirmDialog if nothing is left using it. Found by the stale-items audit (assets/f140e25c). Owner: "ios should have 1:1 parity with the web app". Needs the Mac.
